. Both arms must land together.\n(c) MARKER_KEY (envelope e7bd57fd4): alert-commander derives <nominal_tick> inconsistently between its published-marker key and its notebook header (c263/c264 correct, c265 wrote 03:20 where nominal was 03:15). MARKER_KEY is a cross-tick dedup mechanism, so a mis-derived key silently stops the gate from gating; failure mode is a DOUBLE PUBLISH to a real channel. No damage yet. Folded here ONLY because the envelope claims the same one-line consumer fix closes both (b) and (c) -- architect MUST verify that claim before scoping and split it out if it does not hold.\nFIX SHAPE UNCHANGED (settled at the migrated po_fold_20260825): drop the key lookup, take the NEWEST cycle-snapshot-*.json inside the <=7min freshness gate both copies already specify.\nSTILL DO NOT: (i) round the producer's filename to the nominal tick -- already withdrawn; it makes the producer's name collide with the prior day's EXACTLY rather than approximately. (ii) Widen the prune age threshold -- the prune window (1440 min) EQUALS the filename namespace period (1440 min) by construction, so every HH:MM name has a same-named prior-day twin alive in its final minutes; widening makes it worse.\nRECURRENCE: the 6 cowork-fire envelopes this tick report cycle_snapshot_promoted=false on the 36th-41st consecutive tick. cycle-snapshot-latest.json still tick=00:00 created_at=2026-08-23T00:07:50Z (~75h stale)."
