    "status_note": "MINTED by po triage 2026-08-26T03:48Z from context-bloat-backstop-hook envelope 43ceb6c06 (class=skill-file, reason='line-cap,byte-cap', action_required=prune_or_split). Dedup-checked against the four existing CLEAN-CTXBLOAT-* skill rows -- no row covers this file.\nPRIORITISED ABOVE the routine ctxbloat P3 for two reasons, not just size: (1) at 3.65x the line cap and 3.37x the byte cap this is the largest single breach among the currently-open ctxbloat rows (compare notebook-write SKILL 215L/13016B and cron-cowork-team SKILL 242L/14279B, both P3); (2) CLAUDE.md makes this file a MANDATORY pre-spawn read for every router session (step 2.5, PRE-CLAIM), so its bytes are paid on every dispatch, not lazily.\nSPLIT SHAPE ALREADY EXISTS AND SHOULD BE EXTENDED, NOT REINVENTED: this skill already ships a CARD.md hot-path companion, and CLAUDE.md already routes the hot path to it ('full claim call + claimed/re-entrant/peer-collision outcomes: CARD.md (hot path); full spec: sibling SKILL.md'). So the correct action is to move the remaining cold-path spec bulk OUT of SKILL.md rather than to prune content away -- the hot/cold split is designed, only the migration is incomplete.\nDO NOT prune by deleting the claim outcome semantics or the Step 0a/Phase A/Phase A.5/Step 2.4/Phase B ordering: memory records three separate incidents caused by sessions acting on a partial reading of this exact gate sequence (feedback_step24_cowork_collision_probe_ttl_exceeds_cadence_daily_false_positive, feedback_phaseb_intent_key_is_freeform_so_two_sessions_run_same_agent_concurrently, feedback_router_hand_dispatch_bypasses_deps_satisfied_gate).\nCOORDINATE WITH: UC-RDL-P4B-DOC-CUTOVER (backlog, developer) already plans a CLAUDE.md + dispatch-claim/{CARD.md,SKILL.md} cutover to dispatch_preflight. If that lands first it may subsume most of this file; check it before starting so this is not two rewrites of the same doc.\nAC: both caps satisfied (<=200L, <=12000B) on SKILL.md with